    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288-a4">

                <pb facs="0561" n="427" xml:id="pg427"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Incloaure 4 in No. 133.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Maury to Mr.
                            Restrepo.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 31,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I thank your excellency for your courteous
                    note of the 30th instant, received just now.</p>
                <p>I am relieved to understand from it that when the most excellent President of
                    Colombia, Señor Doctor D. Rafael Nuñez, said in his late message to the national
                    congress that a wide avenue had been opened to the cupidity of foreign
                    speculators, supported by governments which are often not inspired by the
                    wholesome principles of justice, the most excellent President intended no
                    reference to that of the United States as one of those misguided
                    governments.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dabney H.
                            Maury.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
